The \emph{conjugacy classes} of $S_{n}$, the symmetric group on $n$ elements,
are determined by their \emph{cycle structure}. All elements of a class have
the same cycle structure; all elements with the same cycle structure belong to
the same class.

\begin{definition}
The \emph{cycle structure} is defined as the set of non-negative
integers$\{\left.  \U{3bd} _{j}\right\vert j=1,2,...,n\}$, where $\U{3bd}
_{j}$ is the number of $j$-cycles in the unique resolution of a permutation
into non-overlapping cycles. Note that
\begin{equation}
\sum_{1\leq j\leq r}j\U{3bd} _{j}=n.
\end{equation}

\end{definition}

An alternative characterisation of the classes is in terms of the non-negative
integers$\{\left.
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{j}\right\vert j=1,2,...,n\}$, where
\begin{equation}%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{s}=\sum_{s\leq j\leq n}v_{j}%
\end{equation}
it is evident that%
\begin{equation}
\sum_{1\leq j\leq n}%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{j}=n
\end{equation}
and $%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{1}\geq%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{2}\geq...\geq%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{n}\geq0$, i.e. the set $\{\left.
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{j}\right\vert j=1,2,...,n\}$ is a \emph{partition} of $n$.

\begin{enumerate}
\item \emph{The classes can be labeled by the partitions of }$n$\emph{;}

\item \emph{There are as many classes as partitions of }$n$\emph{;}

\item \emph{The cycle structure can be deduced from }$\U{3bd} _{j}=%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{j}-%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{j+1}$\emph{ (with }$%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{n+1}=0$\emph{).}
\end{enumerate}

A useful and widely adopted pictorial \emph{notation for partitions }is
provided by\emph{Young Diagrams}. The Young diagram corresponding to the
partition $\{\left.
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{j}\right\vert j=1,2,...,n\}$ of $n$ consists of left-justified rows of $%
%TCIMACRO{\U{3bc} }%
%BeginExpansion
\mu
%EndExpansion
_{j}$-boxes stacked in decreasing order of length. This definition is best
understood by way of a concrete example:

\begin{example}
$n=5.$ $g_{k}$ is the number of elements in a class with cycle structure
labelled $v_{j}:$
\begin{equation}%
\begin{array}
[c]{ccccc}%
\text{Partition\quad} & \text{Short Form} & \text{Young Tableaux} &
\quad\text{Cycle Structure} & g_{k}=\left.  \overset{}{n!}\right/
%TCIMACRO{\tprod \limits_{1\leq j\leq n}}%
%BeginExpansion
{\textstyle\prod\limits_{1\leq j\leq n}}
%EndExpansion
j^{v_{j}}\left(  \U{3bd} _{j}!\right)
\end{array}
\end{equation}%
\begin{align}
&
\begin{array}
[c]{ccccc}%
5+0+0+0+0\qquad & \left[  5,0^{4}\right]  \qquad\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\qquad & \fbox{$%
\begin{array}
